    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d128">

                <pb facs="0223" n="201" sameAs="frus:frus1951v02/pg201"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/12–851: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the United States Representative at the United Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Austin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-12-08T23:27:00-05:00">December 8,
                            1951—11:27 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Gadel 396. Re Delga 565,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d128-f1"/> 571. Authorization
                    requested Delga 571 granted. In any exercise
                    para 3 discretion Del will wish consider together with other elements whether
                    reaction to negative vote will endanger 36.90 this year or make subsequent
                    reduction to 33⅓ more difficult as well as possible consequences US
                    intransigence this issue for overall political objectives this and following
                        GA’s.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d128-f1" n="1" xml:id="d128-f1-content">
